%% Successful public edit sequence
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  actor Caller as Application code
  participant API as CanvasEditPort
  participant EK as EditKernel
  participant Store as DocumentStoreKernel
  participant Selection as SelectionKernel
  participant Sparse as Sparse edit journal
  participant Draft as DraftDocument fallback
  participant Handle as CanvasEdit handle
  participant Touched as TouchedSet
  participant CC as CommitCompiler
  participant Applier as CommitApplier
  participant Effects as CommitEffects
  participant Spatial as SpatialKernel
  participant Frame as FrameEngine
  participant Events as EventBuffer
  participant Runtime as RuntimeRoot
  participant Signals as Public state/effects

  Caller->>API: edit(fn)
  API->>EK: open synchronous edit session
  EK->>EK: reject disposed or nested edit
  EK->>Store: read committed sparse facts
  Store-->>EK: committed summary, rows, resource facts, revisions
  EK->>Selection: read selected ids and selectionRevision
  Selection-->>EK: selection snapshot for sparse effects
  EK->>Sparse: open callback-local sparse journal
  EK->>Handle: bind live handle to session
  EK-->>Caller: invoke fn(handle)

  activate Handle
  Caller->>Handle: synchronous CanvasEdit mutations
  Handle->>Sparse: record ordinary document/resource mutations and selection requests
  Sparse->>Touched: record exact sparse mutation facts
  opt explicit readDraftDocument or replaceDraftDocument
    Handle->>Draft: materialize committed projection and replay sparse journal
    Draft->>Touched: record materialized fallback facts
  end
  Handle-->>Caller: mutation results
  deactivate Handle

  Caller-->>EK: callback result
  EK->>EK: reject Future result before success path
  Note over EK: If the callback returns a Future, rollback applies and no commit work runs.
  EK->>CC: compile touched set, revisions, invalidation, repaint intent
  Touched-->>CC: exact changed state
  EK->>Store: prepare sparse commit or materialized accepted document
  Store-->>EK: prepared accepted document facts
  CC->>Effects: prepare typed RepaintIntent and invalidation effects
  CC->>Events: stage commit event buffer
  Note over Events: Low-level CanvasEdit commits stage no user action events.

  CC->>Applier: hand off compiled CommitPlan
  Applier->>Selection: prepare accepted selection effects before store install
  Selection-->>Applier: prepared selection accepted
  Applier->>Store: install prepared sparse/materialized document atomically
  Applier->>Selection: install prepared selection effects atomically
  Store->>Store: replace committed tables and revision state
  Selection->>Selection: replace selected ids and selectionRevision from prepared ids
  Note over Applier,Selection: Atomic install is the cross-owner commit boundary.
  Store-->>Applier: committed revision facts
  Selection-->>Applier: committed selection revision facts
  Applier-->>Runtime: committed runtime facts

  EK->>Handle: close session and mark handle stale
  Note over Handle: Any operation after callback throws StateError.
  Runtime->>Runtime: enter one post-commit delivery guard
  Runtime->>Spatial: apply sealed SpatialDeliveryEffect
  Runtime->>Effects: release sealed resource/session targets
  Runtime->>Frame: publish root repaint frame, then bridged surface frame
  Runtime->>Signals: publish one CanvasRuntimeState
  Runtime->>Events: emit finalized synchronous action intent
  Runtime->>Effects: notify non-empty CommitEffectObserver
  Runtime->>Runtime: clear delivery guard
  Note over Runtime,Effects: Resource, frame, state, action, and observer callbacks see installed facts and the closed handle, while their failures retain accepted state according to their owner boundary.
  EK-->>API: return callback result
  API-->>Caller: callback result
